  "verbalization": "Tamulamide B is shown to have a target relationship with MIP, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and Sophoradiol. All three of these entities are ultimately targeted by Carboxylesterase 2, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the enzyme. The evidence indicates that Tamulamide B may act through a shared pathway, where the target molecules are processed by Carboxylesterase 2, potentially through a common intermediate or a shared metabolic pathway. The presence of multiple targets that ultimately converge on Carboxylesterase 2 suggests a possible role in the enzyme's catalytic activity or in the regulation of downstream pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Tamulamide B may exert its effects by modulating the activity of Carboxylesterase 2, either directly or indirectly through the intermediates it targets.",
